WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:03.430
[MUSIC PLAYING]

00:00:08.922 --> 00:00:11.380
SPEAKER: Open the Cloud Storage
browser in the Google Cloud

00:00:11.380 --> 00:00:14.680
Platform Console and
click Create bucket.

00:00:14.680 --> 00:00:16.836
Give the bucket a
globally unique name.

00:00:16.836 --> 00:00:18.460
This name is publicly
visible, so don't

00:00:18.460 --> 00:00:20.390
include sensitive information.

00:00:20.390 --> 00:00:22.090
Choose Regional
for storage class,

00:00:22.090 --> 00:00:24.160
and choose us-east1
for location.

00:00:24.160 --> 00:00:26.980
Click Create, which
will create your bucket.

00:00:26.980 --> 00:00:29.230
Now that we've created a
bucket, let's upload an image

00:00:29.230 --> 00:00:30.470
into the new bucket.

00:00:30.470 --> 00:00:34.007
Click Upload files and select
the file you want to store.

00:00:34.007 --> 00:00:35.590
After the upload
completes, you should

00:00:35.590 --> 00:00:37.870
see the file name, size,
type, and last modified

00:00:37.870 --> 00:00:40.000
date in the bucket.

00:00:40.000 --> 00:00:42.550
In order to share the file,
create a publicly accessible

00:00:42.550 --> 00:00:44.260
URL for it.

00:00:44.260 --> 00:00:46.450
Click the dropdown menu
associated with the file

00:00:46.450 --> 00:00:48.880
and select Edit permissions.

00:00:48.880 --> 00:00:50.800
Click the Add item button.

00:00:50.800 --> 00:00:52.660
In the new row that's
added, enter User

00:00:52.660 --> 00:00:54.070
for the Entity column.

00:00:54.070 --> 00:00:56.260
Enter allUsers in
the Name column,

00:00:56.260 --> 00:00:58.870
and enter Reader in
the Access column.

00:00:58.870 --> 00:01:01.050
Click Save.

00:01:01.050 --> 00:01:03.480
You'll now see there's a
link icon for the object.

00:01:03.480 --> 00:01:06.180
Clicking it will reveal
the object's public URL.

00:01:06.180 --> 00:01:08.140
Now your file is online
for everyone to see.

00:01:08.140 --> 00:01:09.040
Congratulations.

00:01:09.040 --> 00:01:12.390
[MUSIC PLAYING]

